# Universal Python Standards & Strict Linter

All Python code must adhere to the universal styleguide at `~/dev/agent-dev-harness/python-styleguide/python-styleguide.md`.

## Typing & Models
- Modern typing: `list[str]`, `dict[str, int]`, `X | None`. Never import `List`, `Dict`, `Optional`, or `Union` from `typing`.
- Abstract types come from `collections.abc` (`Sequence`, `Mapping`, `Iterable`, `Callable`), not `typing`.
- Accept widest types (`Sequence`), return narrowest concrete types (`list`, `dict`).
- Structured data uses `pydantic.BaseModel` with `model_config = ConfigDict(strict=True, extra="forbid", frozen=True)`.
- All config and environment variables flow through `pydantic_settings.BaseSettings`. Never use `os.environ` or `os.getenv`.
- Read config once at the process entry point; pass it down as an explicit constructor parameter.

## Architecture & Layering
- Keep pure business logic completely separate from I/O and orchestration.
- Pure logic (`core/` or `libs/`) must never import frameworks, network clients, storage, databases, clock, or randomness.
- Imports point strictly downward toward pure logic. Never use lazy imports to bypass circular dependencies.

## Docstrings & Comments
- Concise prose only. Never use `Args:`, `Returns:`, or `Raises:` section blocks (types and names already state them).
- Function/class docstring limit: soft cap 8 lines, hard cap 20 lines.
- Docstrings must never exceed the length of the function body (`DOC003`).
- Use all lowercase for python code comments.

## Strict Verification Before Reporting Done
Before completing any task or marking work as done that touched Python files git would commit, lint them with the agent-dev-harness baseline. Run both from the repo root:

```bash
uvx ruff@0.16.4 check --config ~/dev/agent-dev-harness/python-styleguide/ruff-base.toml <files>
python3 ~/dev/agent-dev-harness/python-styleguide/docstring_length.py <files>
```

1. Add `--fix` to the ruff command for safe autofixes.
2. Fix all remaining ruff and docstring violations before concluding.

Skip this for scratch scripts outside a git repo or in gitignored paths, such as `/tmp` helpers for ad hoc checks. The `stop` hook runs the same two checks on committable files and re-prompts with any findings.
